    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Let me create a comprehensive summary of the implementation:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval` as requested. Here's what was added:\n\n### **1. CLI Changes** (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`)\n- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option (can be given multiple times)\n- Created `parseThresholds()` function to:\n  - Parse format: `exact_match=0.9`\n  - Validate metric names: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`\n  - Validate values are between 0 and 1\n  - Exit with code 2 for malformed thresholds or unknown metrics\n- Modified `runEvalCommand()` to:\n  - Pass thresholds to `generateReport()`\n  - Exit with code 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass\n\n### **2. Core Logic** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`)\n- Updated `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n- When thresholds are provided:\n  - Adds `passed` field (true if all thresholds pass)\n  - Adds `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries per threshold\n  - Treats null scores as failing their threshold\n- Without thresholds, report structure remains unchanged for backward compatibility\n\n### **3. Reporting** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`)\n- Updated `toMarkdown()` to include \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status\n- JSON reports automatically include `passed` and `thresholds` fields\n\n### **4. Tests** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`)\n- Added comprehensive tests for:\n  - Passing thresholds\n  - Failing thresholds\n  - Null score handling\n  - Backward compatibility (no thresholds = no passed field)\n\n### **Verification Results**\nAll custom verification tests pass, demonstrating:\n- \u2705 Thresholds properly evaluated\n- \u2705 JSON reports include threshold results\n- \u2705 Markdown reports show PASS/FAIL status\n- \u2705 Exit codes work correctly (0 for pass, 1 for fail, 2 for invalid input)\n- \u2705 Backward compatible (works with/without thresholds)\n\nThe feature is complete and ready for use!",
